From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 06:59:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath10k: snoc: keep the copy engine IRQs balanced across
 a restart

The copy engine IRQs are left enabled across a firmware restart: hif_stop
skips disabling them when CRASH_FLUSH is set, and hif_start skips
enabling them when RECOVERY is set. The two flags do not always pair up.
The "fw down" indication sets RECOVERY even when the device is not
started, for example when the modem restarts while the interface is down
or before the first interface up. hif_stop has disabled the IRQs in that
case, so the next hif_start leaves them disabled. The firmware start then
falls back to polling for the HTC control response and fails with
"failed to connect htt (-110)", and Wi-Fi stays down until reboot.

On a comma four this happened after a modem restart while wlan0 was
down.

Track whether the IRQs are enabled and enable or disable them only on a
real change, keeping them enabled across a crash restart as before.

Signed-off-by: Adeeb Shihadeh <adeeb@comma.ai>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c | 9 ++++++---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.h | 1 +
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
index 8de133fe2a..ab5b11dbd4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.c
@@ -925,7 +925,11 @@ static void ath10k_snoc_buffer_cleanup(struct ath10k *ar)
 
 static void ath10k_snoc_hif_stop(struct ath10k *ar)
 {
-	if (!test_bit(ATH10K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ar->dev_flags))
+	struct ath10k_snoc *ar_snoc = ath10k_snoc_priv(ar);
+
+	/* IRQs are left enabled when we restart due to a firmware crash */
+	if (!test_bit(ATH10K_FLAG_CRASH_FLUSH, &ar->dev_flags) &&
+	    test_and_clear_bit(ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_IRQS_ENABLED, &ar_snoc->flags))
 		ath10k_snoc_irq_disable(ar);
 
 	ath10k_core_napi_sync_disable(ar);
@@ -941,8 +945,7 @@ static int ath10k_snoc_hif_start(struct ath10k *ar)
 
 	netif_threaded_enable(ar->napi_dev);
 	ath10k_core_napi_enable(ar);
-	/* IRQs are left enabled when we restart due to a firmware crash */
-	if (!test_bit(ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_RECOVERY, &ar_snoc->flags))
+	if (!test_and_set_bit(ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_IRQS_ENABLED, &ar_snoc->flags))
 		ath10k_snoc_irq_enable(ar);
 	ath10k_snoc_rx_post(ar);
 
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.h
index 46574fd8f8..42dbab3c1e 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath10k/snoc.h
@@ -52,6 +52,7 @@ enum ath10k_snoc_flags {
 	ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_RECOVERY,
 	ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_8BIT_HOST_CAP_QUIRK,
 	ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_SKIP_HOST_CAP_QUIRK,
+	ATH10K_SNOC_FLAG_IRQS_ENABLED,
 };
 
 struct clk_bulk_data;
